[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444085513","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4444085513","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4444085513,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCONdCQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T18:26:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T18:30:06Z","body":"I'm not sure this is the right fix, as large boxes still won't be subdivided enough to look good when AreaLight3Ds that cast shadows affect them.\r\n\r\nThis also greatly increases the polygon count of each BoxMesh (from 12 to 108 primitives), which can reduce performance in scenes with lots of BoxMeshes (especially smaller ones, with triangles becoming smaller than 2×2). We might get fewer complaints about AreaLight3D shadows, but instead, we'd get complaints of performance regressions when upgrading test scenes that use lots of BoxMeshes.\r\n\r\nI would only change the documentation instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444085513/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444426116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4444426116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4444426116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCOiPhA","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T19:12:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T19:12:19Z","body":"> I'm not sure this is the right fix, as large boxes still won't be subdivided enough to look good when AreaLight3Ds that cast shadows affect them.\r\n\r\nIts not the size of the box that matters so much as the size of the individual triangles in the Camera frustum. We discussed doing 2 subdivisions in the meeting since it should look good in 99% of cases and have no performance impact. So, there is always the potential for issues if the light is sufficiently close to the box or if the box is sufficiently large, but we care most about the common case, not the rare case. \r\n\r\n> This also greatly increases the polygon count of each BoxMesh (from 12 to 108 primitives), which can reduce performance in scenes with lots of BoxMeshes (especially smaller ones, with triangles becoming smaller than 2×2). We might get fewer complaints about AreaLight3D shadows, but instead, we'd get complaints of performance regressions when upgrading test scenes that use lots of BoxMeshes.\r\n\r\nRemember that GPUs are massively parallel processors, almost all GPUs process 32 or 64 threads at a time. If you have less vertices than the number of threads, then increasing vertex count makes no difference. Also remember, its vertex count, not polygon count that matters in this case. This PR goes from 8 vertices to 56. So on a lot of hardware it won't make a difference (the threads would be sitting idle anyway). And on some hardware the number of invocations goes up by 1. In all cases the difference is likely to be negligible (except for extreme cases where the vertex shader is doing very complicated work).\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444426116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445218275","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4445218275","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4445218275,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCPSl4w","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T21:07:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T21:07:42Z","body":"As discussed in the meeting, we can't change the default on the `BoxMesh` directly because it will change behaviour on existing projects:\r\n\r\nGodot 4.7 beta 1| This PR\r\n--|--\r\n<img width=\"1282\" height=\"789\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7486bbe0-f63d-4f22-864f-79c4c529854d\" />| <img width=\"1282\" height=\"789\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e648b63-78b2-4778-99f8-c226be26e650\" />\r\n\r\nInstead, we need to find a way to change the number of subdivs only on new `BoxMesh` resources that the editor creates.\r\n\r\n(`BoxMesh` is used in existing projects for quite a lot more than just test scenes and is likely used by games that depend on the specific number of vertices of the existing default.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445218275/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445329837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4445329837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4445329837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCPZZrQ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T21:25:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T21:26:33Z","body":"> Instead, we need to find a way to change the number of subdivs only on new BoxMesh resources that the editor creates.\r\n\r\nThis would be pretty surprising behavior IMO where different BoxMeshes in the same project behave differently without user intervention.\r\n\r\nA safer approach is to enable the new behavior only for new projects created in Godot versions that include this change, and preexisting projects keep the previous behavior as a fallback (and can opt in the new behavior for all their BoxMeshes by changing a project setting). We have some logic to handle this pattern.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445329837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445648967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4445648967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4445648967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCPs4Rw","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T22:21:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T22:21:12Z","body":"Changing the defaults of BoxMesh, even if gated by a project setting, will still break compatibility of resources that are shared between projects. Say I have a packed scene and scripts in one project and I move them to another project and get an out of bounds error in the other project because it doesn’t use the same project setting configuration.\r\n\r\nEspecially if this is an asset produced by someone else that would be difficult to debug (who would think that a primitive mesh would have a different number of vertices in one project than the exact same asset when loaded in a different project?)\r\n\r\nThe bugs introduced by changing default values sound worse to me than the bugs caused by the current defaults.\r\n\r\n> This would be pretty surprising behavior IMO where different BoxMeshes in the same project behave differently without user intervention.\r\n\r\nI don’t see this as something that would be a common surprise in practice and I also don’t see that it would be a real problem, in spite of it possibly being more surprising than the surprise that BoxMesh would ever be created with more than 0 subdivisions without user intervention.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445648967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445824051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4445824051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4445824051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCP3kMw","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T22:57:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T22:57:09Z","body":"this is just masking a problem, it's Better for somebody to find the problem, open a bug report and get pointed to the docs with the bug report closed.\r\n\r\nAs pointed out in the OG issue ALOD also doesn't like respecting the tessellation either so this will be present in production levels as well and this NEEDS to be made clear in the docs, I'd also add this issue as a Warning to the Description of Area Lights, which should minimize the number of bug reports a bit.\r\n\r\nThe only proper fix for this issue would be to somehow detect under tessellation and tessellate, but that is a much more difficult task to do (and do well) and it may come with a bunch of caveats of it's own","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445824051/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4506604788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4506604788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4506604788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDJ1U9A","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T09:14:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T09:14:22Z","body":"Seems like there's enough pushback on this. I have opened a documentation PR instead","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4506604788/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4509640321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4509640321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4509640321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDMumgQ","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T15:13:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T15:13:10Z","body":"Better documentation sounds like a good improvement. I still think it could be possible to resolve the issue by changing editor behaviour instead of changing resource defaults, but there is pushback from akien-mga about this. It might not be worth exploring this option if it won’t get merged out of principle…","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4509640321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4509722142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119441#issuecomment-4509722142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119441","id":4509722142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDMzmHg","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T15:22:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T15:22:31Z","body":"I agree with you, but this isn't a hill i'm willing to die on x)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4509722142/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]